From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reindert Pelsma <reindert.pelsma@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 17:10:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] ui/gtk: switch to the guest's display when it first
 goes live

The owner photographed his screen and reported no Mint desktop.  The
desktop was running fine.  The window was on the wrong console.

QEMU's emulated VGA is console 0 and nvkvm's scanout console registers
second.  ui/gtk.c builds one notebook page per console in index order
and then never changes the current page, so the guest desktop renders
perfectly on a tab nobody is looking at -- and from outside, a window
showing a boot console is indistinguishable from a hung guest.  That
cost real debugging time before anyone thought to press View -> Show
Tabs.

This was previously written down as "no API for a device to request a
page change".  True of upstream QEMU, but we build QEMU from source and
already patch it, so the constraint was "not exposed", not "not
possible".

WHEN a console goes live: every console starts on a PLACEHOLDER surface
("Guest has not initialized the display (yet)"), so for the surface
paths the first non-placeholder surface is the moment real content
arrives.  For the GL paths a scanout texture is real content by
definition.  gd_switch() and its siblings already run at exactly those
points, so no new plumbing is needed to find the moment.

WHAT it does is a latch, not a policy engine.  Fire only while the
window is still on the page it opened on (page 0), only for a page
above it, and at most once:

  * the VGA going live is page 0, so it cannot consume the one shot;
  * nvkvm going live is a page above 0, so it does;
  * once fired -- or once the user has moved the tab themselves -- the
    condition can never hold again, so a manual tab choice is never
    overridden and the user is never dragged back;
  * with -vga none there is only page 0, so it is a no-op.

Three required behaviours, no new state to decide them.  That is the
whole reason for phrasing it as a condition on the notebook rather than
as a rule about devices: there is nothing to get out of sync.

WHERE: all five GTK entry points, not just gd_switch().  This is the
part worth not "simplifying" later.  NVKVM_PRESENT_MODE=readback goes
through gd_switch(), but NVKVM_PRESENT_MODE=gl -- the documented 60fps
path -- goes through the egl and gl-area scanout paths instead and would
never reach gd_switch() at all.  A gd_switch()-only fix works in
whichever mode happens to be under test and silently does nothing in the
other, which is worse than not fixing it: it turns a visible bug into an
intermittent one.  (gd_egl_scanout_dmabuf() and
gd_gl_area_scanout_dmabuf() both funnel into their *_scanout_texture
counterparts, so hooking the texture entry covers the dma-buf entry.)

The latch lives in include/ui/gtk.h so the surface path and both GL
paths share one, rather than one per file -- three latches would fire up
to three times.

It logs one line when it fires.  A window moving on its own is
surprising if you are not expecting it, and this is the only record that
it happened.

Only compiled into a build configured --enable-gtk, i.e.
NVKVM_QEMU_UI=1.  The default headless build applies this patch and
never compiles a line of it.

Verified on the physical display, measured rather than argued:
  * fires: "nvkvm: guest display is live -- switched window to console
    page 1";
  * fires exactly once -- `grep -c` over the run is 1, after further
    desktop activity and three more screendumps;
  * -vga none: zero notices, QEMU alive, desktop still captures at
    1920x1080.
Desktop confirmed live on that console (three screendumps four seconds
apart, three distinct checksums) with Firefox, Nemo and glxgears
rendering.  Full tests/validate.sh: 28 PASS, 0 FAIL, 0 SKIP.

NOT upstreamable as written, and should not be sent as-is: it is
nvkvm-specific policy ("the interesting console is the one that is not
the boot VGA") hardcoded into a generic front end, with an nvkvm-branded
symbol and an nvkvm-branded log line.  The underlying gap is real and
general, though -- any device whose console registers after the VGA has
this problem, and upstream has no way for a console to say "I have
something worth looking at".  A `dpy_console_request_focus()`-shaped
mechanism, with the front end owning the policy, would be the
upstreamable version.  Until someone writes that, this stays downstream.
---
 include/ui/gtk.h | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 ui/gtk-egl.c     |  6 ++++++
 ui/gtk-gl-area.c |  6 ++++++
 ui/gtk.c         |  6 ++++++
 4 files changed, 48 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/ui/gtk.h b/include/ui/gtk.h
index 5c9c34a069..b8b083b9db 100644
--- a/include/ui/gtk.h
+++ b/include/ui/gtk.h
@@ -162,6 +162,36 @@ void gd_update_windowsize(VirtualConsole *vc);
 void gd_update_monitor_refresh_rate(VirtualConsole *vc, GtkWidget *widget);
 void gd_hw_gl_flushed(void *vc);
 
+/*
+ * nvkvm: one-shot auto-switch to the guest's GPU head.  Full rationale is in
+ * this patch's header.  Declared here because the surface path (ui/gtk.c) and
+ * both GL paths (ui/gtk-egl.c, ui/gtk-gl-area.c) all need it, and the latch has
+ * to be shared between them rather than per-file.
+ */
+extern bool nvkvm_gd_auto_switched;
+
+static inline void nvkvm_gd_maybe_autoswitch(VirtualConsole *vc)
+{
+    GtkNotebook *nb;
+    gint page;
+
+    if (nvkvm_gd_auto_switched || !vc || !vc->s || !vc->s->notebook ||
+        !vc->tab_item) {
+        return;
+    }
+    nb = GTK_NOTEBOOK(vc->s->notebook);
+    page = gtk_notebook_page_num(nb, vc->tab_item);
+    /* page < 0 means this console was detached into its own window. */
+    if (page > 0 && gtk_notebook_get_current_page(nb) == 0) {
+        nvkvm_gd_auto_switched = true;
+        gtk_notebook_set_current_page(nb, page);
+        /* One line, once: the window moving on its own is surprising if you
+         * are not expecting it, and this is the only record that it happened. */
+        fprintf(stderr, "nvkvm: guest display is live -- switched window to "
+                        "console page %d\n", page);
+    }
+}
+
 /* ui/gtk-egl.c */
 void gd_egl_init(VirtualConsole *vc);
 void gd_egl_draw(VirtualConsole *vc);
diff --git a/ui/gtk-egl.c b/ui/gtk-egl.c
index adc81f34b1..8e72905032 100644
--- a/ui/gtk-egl.c
+++ b/ui/gtk-egl.c
@@ -211,6 +211,10 @@ void gd_egl_switch(DisplayChangeListener *dcl,
         gd_update_windowsize(vc);
     }
 
+    if (!surface_is_placeholder(surface)) {
+        nvkvm_gd_maybe_autoswitch(vc);   /* nvkvm: head just went live */
+    }
+
     eglMakeCurrent(qemu_egl_display, EGL_NO_SURFACE, EGL_NO_SURFACE,
                    EGL_NO_CONTEXT);
 }
@@ -260,6 +264,8 @@ void gd_egl_scanout_texture(DisplayChangeListener *dcl,
     gtk_egl_set_scanout_mode(vc, true);
     egl_fb_setup_for_tex(&vc->gfx.guest_fb, backing_width, backing_height,
                          backing_id, false);
+
+    nvkvm_gd_maybe_autoswitch(vc);   /* nvkvm: a scanout texture is real content */
 }
 
 void gd_egl_scanout_dmabuf(DisplayChangeListener *dcl,
diff --git a/ui/gtk-gl-area.c b/ui/gtk-gl-area.c
index 29497019ee..38f7d43995 100644
--- a/ui/gtk-gl-area.c
+++ b/ui/gtk-gl-area.c
@@ -207,6 +207,10 @@ void gd_gl_area_switch(DisplayChangeListener *dcl,
     if (resized) {
         gd_update_windowsize(vc);
     }
+
+    if (!surface_is_placeholder(surface)) {
+        nvkvm_gd_maybe_autoswitch(vc);   /* nvkvm: head just went live */
+    }
 }
 
 static int gd_cmp_gl_context_version(int major, int minor, QEMUGLParams *params)
@@ -311,6 +315,8 @@ void gd_gl_area_scanout_texture(DisplayChangeListener *dcl,
     gtk_gl_area_set_scanout_mode(vc, true);
     egl_fb_setup_for_tex(&vc->gfx.guest_fb, backing_width, backing_height,
                          backing_id, false);
+
+    nvkvm_gd_maybe_autoswitch(vc);   /* nvkvm: a scanout texture is real content */
 }
 
 void gd_gl_area_scanout_disable(DisplayChangeListener *dcl)
diff --git a/ui/gtk.c b/ui/gtk.c
index 7078d89d67..697e441acb 100644
--- a/ui/gtk.c
+++ b/ui/gtk.c
@@ -495,6 +495,8 @@ static void gd_cursor_define(DisplayChangeListener *dcl,
     g_object_unref(cursor);
 }
 
+bool nvkvm_gd_auto_switched;
+
 static void gd_switch(DisplayChangeListener *dcl,
                       DisplaySurface *surface)
 {
@@ -556,6 +558,10 @@ static void gd_switch(DisplayChangeListener *dcl,
     } else {
         gd_update_full_redraw(vc);
     }
+
+    if (!surface_is_placeholder(surface)) {
+        nvkvm_gd_maybe_autoswitch(vc);   /* nvkvm: head just went live */
+    }
 }
 
 static const DisplayChangeListenerOps dcl_ops = {
